        comment     2026-11-21T20:57:24Z
            Slice state inventory (requirements lead): every state is made once at module load; the only run-time reader
            is the restore. Each has one owner after the build; today's writers are listed where there are several.

            | State | Owner (one writer) | Writers today | Readers | Saved |
            | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
            | A door's registration (name, kind) | `door` | `entry`, `entryEffect`, `builder`, `inert` into `entry.ts` `registry` | refusals, surface walk | no |
            | A made value's brand, kind, owner, internals | `made` | `~flow` in 6 files, `~owner` (`definition.ts`, `handles.ts`), `~path`, `~token`; WeakMaps in `flow.ts`, `events.ts`, `machine.ts`, `host/runtime.ts` | `madeOf` | no |
            | Recognition (internals, WrongKind, ForeignToken, Defect) | `madeOf`, a pure read | `config.ts#isToken`, `construction.ts#isMarker`, `machine.ts` `~owner` probe, `compile-names.ts#foreign`, `tokenOf` | every door | no |
            | A definition's schedule declaration | `definition()` | none (new) | `machine()`'s checks, the codec build, later `derive.ts` | no |
            | `Compiled.schedules` (key, selection, reasons) | the compile pass | none (new) | each `Node` schedule (a pointer, not a copy), restore (T118) | no |
            | Schedule construction findings | the twin-row check, one row per reason | `config.ts` body decode (`UnknownField`), `compile-schedules.ts#armingOf`, `Flow.keyed` decode | refusal; later Construction (T22) | no |

            Transition table, `madeOf(kind, owner)(value)`, replacing five scattered checks (an implicit state machine):

            | Read of the brand | Kind | Owner | Result |
            | --- | --- | --- | --- |
            | throws | any | any | one `Defect` finding at the argument's path |
            | false (a copy) | any | any | `WrongKind` |
            | true | other | any | `WrongKind` |
            | true | this | other definition | `ForeignToken` |
            | true | this | this | the internals |

            Seams: where `Compiled` sits after the doors (face or internals) decides how T120's codec checks and every
            `machine.compiled` reader reach it; a schedule key's codec text must equal today's `encodeCanonical` text
            for string keys, so records saved before the slice restore. Resources: T131 touches none; T120 reads the
            store at restore only, through `Fake.storage.put`, and no write path changes, so no fake gap applies.
