    T92
        title       Records decoded into meaning: branded identifiers, each fact stored once, full record decoding
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T118]

        satisfies   [@plan.Runtime.O1]
        description
            Saved records decode through Schemas built from the compiled app, with branded identifiers and each fact
            stored once, so the boot never acts on a record nobody checked.

            **Why now:** @task.V3.T20 hit the failure limit on one class: restore trusted a part of a record nobody
            checked; four reviews each found one more (a `~` name, a key naming another identity, lane keys, context
            bindings). The record Schemas in code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts decode shape only
            (`machine`, `name`, `operation`, `lane` are `Schema.String`), meaning is then checked by hand, and identity
            is stored in both key and content. T20's bindings blocker is parked here as an inverted test (@spec.Records
            R4). It must land before @task.V3.T56 (versions these records) and real storage
            (@task.V3.T58, @task.V3.T28).

            **Read first:** @task.V3.T20 (its 2026-11-18T06:49 field list and 07:05 review), @convention.boundaries.
            Spec: @spec.Records (R4, R5, R9–R11, R14, R15, R17, R20, R21, I1–I3, I5, I8–I10, I14),
            companion `wiki/specs/v3/Records.md`.

            **Build-time choice (@spec.Records companion holes H2 and H11):** (1) `graph` stores other identities'
            wiring a second time. A: derive it at a boot wake from the provider's own record where one exists, saving
            only providers with no record. B: keep `graph` as saved. A keeps each fact in one place; B is needed if a
            boot wake reads the wiring before the provider's record is admitted. Test: trace the boot wake's readers of
            `graph`; if none reads it before admission, take A and plant `graph-stored-twice`. (2) Whether today's saved
            memory holds `Flow.input` fields. Test first: save a fixture whose machine has a `Flow.input` field and read
            the record; if the field is there, step 5 to 6 removes it and the `memory` row reports nothing (as the Spec
            says), otherwise no step row is needed.

            The linked Spec is pre-coding analysis: follow it as best-guess guidance for how to build, not a strict
            contract; it should help a lot. Where building shows it wrong, fix the Spec and log the change
            in `wiki/specs/specs.log`.

            **Supersedes:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#decodeRecords,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#identityIn,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#rowOf,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#rowsRecord,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#laneRecord,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#keyNamesItself,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#encodeLane,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#encodeOwed,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record.ts#rowJson;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record-format.ts#ActorJson,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/record-format.ts#actorOf;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/actor-record.ts#encodeActor,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/actor-record.ts#decodeActor;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/world.ts#actorKey,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/world.ts#laneId,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/world.ts#restoredLaneId,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/world.ts#restoredAttemptId;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/incarnations.ts#boot,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/incarnations.ts#reportUnbound;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/persist.ts#laneWrite,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/persist.ts#owedWrite,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/persist.ts#actorWrite,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/persist.ts#liveText; the boot's writes (`saveOwed`, `saveLane`,
            `incarnations.ts:446-456`). Do not delete it before its replacement lands and the suite passes.

            **Risk:** a Records Spec change, so it gets the whole-system check; the format is internal and unreleased,
            so nothing migrates.

            **Approach:** first, decide with evidence whether an actor record's context bindings can be derived from its
            machine and its ref's input; if so, stop saving them. Then:

            - branded identifiers, each made only by a Schema decode built from Compiled or by the mint (@spec.Records,
              realization: `MachineId`, `ActorName`, `StateName`, `ContractName`, `KeyText`, `AttemptId`,
              `SubjectAddress`, `ShapeStamp`); every saved name resolves through the one reference table (R15), and no
              other code looks a saved name up in a definition;
