        description
            `Fake.storage`, the fake page and `Fake.server` do by default what their real counterparts can do to an app
            (close, refuse after close, hold, hide, answer late or never), so every Story meets the real lifecycle.

            **Why now:** T58's close review found that `dispose({ forget: true })` deleted nothing on real IndexedDB,
            and every Node test passed only because `Fake.storage` never closes; the user made "a fake kinder than the
            real thing" a class every later Task inherits (2026-11-20). @task.V3.T111 runs every fixture in real
            browsers next, so the fakes should fail the same way first.

            **Read first:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/fake.ts,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/host/testing/store-contract.ts, @task.V3.T58 (its close review and fix
            round), @plan.Testing. Blocked by T58, whose fix round adds a store that closes with the services. Spec:
            @spec.Host (R5, R7, I11, I12), companion `wiki/specs/v3/Host.md`; the mutation alphabet the applier
            `Fake.storage.mutate(kind)` reads is @spec.Records.T2.

