    T113
        title       The typed machine: derived types everywhere user code needs them, no hand-written guesses
        status      draft
        priority    high
        blocked_by  [@T57, @T131, @T120]
        satisfies   [@plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Machines.O8]
        description
            Every type user code needs from a definition, machine or contract is derived by Flow, so no handler,
            fragment, helper, mapper or snapshot read types an event, memory, ending or key by hand.

            **Why now:** a snapshot cannot type a schedule's `pausedBy` or a keyed schedule's send key until the
            definition's declaration carries them (@spec.Schedules R16), and every later Task that adds a snapshot field
            (props, emit summary, fragment summary) would otherwise add its own typing path (breakdown review, the
            orchestrator, 2026-11-20). A survey (2026-11-20) found about 100 hand-typed parameters and 6 copied local
            types that nothing checks against a definition: about 45 ending mappers (`E.X.from((v: {…}) => …)`, `{ why:
            string }` about 25 times), 25 memory parameters and 18 event payloads in fragments and helpers outside the
            `on` literal, and duplicated helpers (`byRepo` in `fixtures/sync` and `fixtures/lanes`, `fromAccount` in two
            transfers machines). One class: a type Flow knows, written by hand where inference does not reach; the user
            widened this Task to remove it everywhere (2026-11-20).

            **Read first:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts, @questions.advisor-questions (question 1),
            @plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Machines.O8, @spec.Schedules (R16). Spec: @spec.Types (R1–R3, R7, R8, R9, R10,
            R13–R15, I1–I4, I10, I12, Q19), companion `wiki/specs/v3/Types.md`.

            **Build-time choice (definition findings and tokens, @spec.Types Q12):** the first spike walks today's
            definition findings. For each finding, A: `definition()` still hands out every token (`S`, `E`, `O`) and the
            finding waits for construction's value (Types Q1); B: that finding keeps raising at `definition()`, as a
            wrong-kind argument does. A is correct only if the token's name is known without the failing part (a
            duplicate state name is not: two tokens would share one name). B is correct whenever a token would be
            ambiguous. Test: per finding, a module with `const Idle = X.S.IDLE` at top level; if the token is
            well-defined, take A and assert the module imports; otherwise B, listed in the Spec's construction rows. Q13
            to Q16 are this Task's build rows: compile each `Changes` row as its code lands, record check time per step
            with the construction benches (Q15), and inventory Family D against `derive.ts` (Q16).


            The linked Spec is pre-coding analysis: follow it as best-guess guidance for how to build, not a strict
            contract; it should help a lot. Where building shows it wrong, fix the Spec and log the change
            in `wiki/specs/specs.log`.

            **Supersedes:** code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#Parts,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#BodyOf, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#MachineBody,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#machine, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#erasedBody,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#erasedWhen,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#trustedTokens,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/machine.ts#handled;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/definition.ts#Definition,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/definition.ts#AnyDefinition,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/definition.ts#Machine,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/definition.ts#treeOfDefinition;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/tree.ts#chainOf, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/tree.ts#leafOf
            (replaced by `Node.chain` and `Node.leaf`; the turn walk, their last caller, moves in @task.V3.T119, which
            deletes them); code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/events.ts#codecOf,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/events.ts#trusted;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/contract.ts#trustedAttempt;
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/compile-body.ts#childrenOf,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/compile-body.ts#childNodes,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/compile-body.ts#nodesOf,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/compile-body.ts#tokenMaps; code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/handles.ts#erase;
